  data: {
    LLM: "Don't overbid for the Declarer role unless you hold at least one 3 and several 2s. The widow is small and rarely fixes a terrible hand.\n\nCounting the 3s: There are only four 3s in the deck. If you hold three of them, you control the game. Force opponents to waste their 3s on single cards.\n\nDefensive Lead: As an opponent, lead a combo type the Declarer is likely weak in. If they passed on a pair earlier, keep leading pairs to prevent them from shedding their singles.",
